  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Sambhal Showroom",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Sambhal Showroom\"**\n\nA calm, well-lit showroom for a real workshop: white walls, square photos of each piece, and a royal-navy shopfront with a thread of gold. The pieces lead; type and colour step back so the tray, its size and its price are read first. It sits in the category standard of Indian home-decor shops at the level of Nicobar and Ellementry, played straight, with the bulk offer never more than one tap away.\n\nDensity is generous on a phone first: one idea per section, 72px between sections, hairline rules instead of boxes, photography square and edge-to-edge in its frame. Royal navy carries the brand moments (the fact bar, the fact ribbon, the bulk band, the footer) and zari gold is its ornament, used only on navy. Everything clickable to buy is WhatsApp green. Motion is slow and soft: the hero crossfades between four photos, a single ribbon of shop facts drifts across the screen, sections rise into place once.\n\nThe build refuses the craft-fair page: no cream-on-cream with a giant serif, no icon-card grids, no testimonial props. Every picture that is not a real photo says so on its face.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White ground, warm stone bands, royal navy brand bands with a 3px gold top rule.",
      "Young Serif for headings, Hanken Grotesk for everything a buyer reads to decide, Rozha One for the wordmark only.",
      "Square product photos on one pale field, 4px corners, no card chrome.",
      "WhatsApp green is the only buying colour.",
      "Slow ease-out motion; all of it stops under reduced motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Gold-On-Navy Rule",
        "body": "Zari gold appears only on royal navy. On white it fails contrast and reads as decoration; on light grounds the accent is Antique Bronze.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Green Rule",
        "body": "WhatsApp green is the order button and the order button is WhatsApp green. No other element, state or illustration uses it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Facts-In-Sans Rule",
        "body": "Sizes, prices, minimums and materials are always set in Hanken Grotesk with tabular figures. The serif names things; it never carries a number a buyer must act on, except the ornamental step counters.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Wordmark-Only Rule",
        "body": "Rozha One is the logo. It never sets a headline.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No-Lift Rule",
        "body": "Cards, photos and buttons never take a shadow. Hover is a change of tone or a slow image zoom, not elevation.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use WhatsApp Green (#0f7a4c) for every WhatsApp action and only for those.",
      "**Do** keep Zari Gold (#c9a25a) on Royal Navy (#15214a); use Antique Bronze (#7d5a1c) for links and accents on white or stone.",
      "**Do** show each piece as a square photo on the Photo Field with 4px corners, and put a \"Design picture\" or \"Styled picture\" tag on every picture that is not a real photo.",
      "**Do** set sizes, prices and minimums in Hanken Grotesk with tabular figures.",
      "**Do** separate content with 1px hairline rules and tone bands, 72px between sections.",
      "**Do** use the shared ease-out (cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1)) for every transition, and let reduced motion switch all motion off."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** put gold text or gold rules on white or stone grounds.",
      "**Don't** give cards, photos or buttons a shadow, or wrap products in bordered boxes.",
      "**Don't** build grids of icon cards, testimonial blocks or client-logo strips.",
      "**Don't** set a headline in Rozha One, or a number a buyer acts on in the serif.",
      "**Don't** put a small uppercase label above a headline; tracked uppercase is for footer column heads only.",
      "**Don't** add a second moving element beside the hero slideshow and the fact ribbon; sections rise once and then stay still."
    ]
  }
}